Would those steps be right?
1.  k cordon nodename; 
2. k drain --ignore-daemonsets nodename; 
3. ssh into node; 
4. swapoff -a; 
5. then find swap line in /etc/fstab and comment it out; 
6. run apt-mark unhold kubeadm kubelet kubectl && \
apt-get update && apt-get install -y kubeadm=1.2xx-00 kubelet=1.2x.x-00 kubectl=1.2x.x-00&& \ apt-mark hold kubeadm  kubelet kubectl 
7. sudo systemctl daemon-reload
8. sudo systemctl restart kubelet
9. exit ssh
10.k uncordon node
